IMPORT prelude

-- Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW), with the Workplace Injury Management and Workers Compensation Act 1998 (NSW)
-- and the Workers Compensation Regulation 2016 (NSW) -- compensation for an injured worker, and the duties of the
-- worker, the employer and the insurer around a claim.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Acts' own actors and terms: "the worker", "the employer", "the
-- insurer", "the dependants", "the worker's legal personal representative". The questions are in three seat layers,
-- which IMPORT this module and restate no rule: nsw-wc-seat.l4 (the injured worker, and on the worker's death the
-- dependants), nsw-wc-seat-insurer.l4 (the insurer) and nsw-wc-seat-employer.l4 (the employer).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. 1987 Act: s 25(1), (2), (4), (5); s 26; s 32A (first and second entitlement periods; worker with
-- high needs; worker with highest needs); s 33; s 34(1AA), (1); s 36; s 37; s 38(1)-(7); s 38A(1); s 39; s 52; s 59A;
-- s 66(1), (1A), (2)(c)-(h), (2A), (3); s 82A (as a declared factor), s 82C(a); Schedule 3 cl 2(1), (2), (4), cl 8,
-- cl 9 (as a fact). 1998 Act: ss 44(1), (2), (4); s 48; s 48A; s 49; s 254; s 261; s 264(1), (2), (4); ss 267, 268,
-- 269; s 274(1)-(4) with s 275(2) and s 276(1); s 283(1) (the offence for s 274). Regulation: cl 8AB; cl 35(1)-(3);
-- cl 36; Schedule 5 (the
-- penalty notice amounts, quoted in the consequences only).
-- Duties and deadlines are regulative rules (DEONTIC); amounts and dates are functions.
--
-- NOT COVERED, answered with an explicit value: the s 66(2)(a) and (b) amounts for more than 10% and not more than 50%
-- impairment (the formulas were lost when the corpus converted the text; only "where D is ..." survives); injuries
-- received before 21 October 2019; police officers, paramedics, firefighters and coal miners (Schedule 6 keeps the
-- 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from their injuries).
--
-- FIGURES. Every dollar amount of the 1987 Act used here is indexed by an order of the Authority (SIRA) that is not
-- deposited: s 25 and s 34 under Division 6 (ss 79-82), the s 38(3)(b) $155 under s 82B, the s 38A $788.32 under
-- s 82BA, and the s 66(2) amounts under Division 6B (s 82F). Each is an INPUT, and the seat layers default it to the
-- figure the deposited text states. The PIAWE minimum of $155 (Regulation cl 8AB) and the funeral maximum of $15,000
-- (s 26) are not indexed by the deposited texts and are used as stated.
--
-- Edition: 1987 Act act-1987-070 (version 2023-10-30), 1998 Act act-1998-086 (version 2024-07-01), Regulation
-- sl-2016-0559 (version 2024-07-24), each from the Open Australian Legal Corpus as at 10 March 2025, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-1987-070.txt,
-- ../../../workplace-injury-management-and-workers-compensation-act-1998/registers/source-bundle/act-1998-086.txt and
-- ../../../workers-compensation-regulation-2016/registers/source-bundle/sl-2016-0559.txt. NOT the current official
-- text; it may be out of date. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited texts with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18.
-- No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Workers Compensation Act 1987 (NSW) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- READINGS (the Interpretation Act 1987 (NSW) is not deposited). "Within N days after" a day ends on the day N days
-- later (the day itself excluded). "Within N months after" a day ends on the same date N months later, or the last day
-- of that month if it has no such date. "A period of N years commencing on" a day includes that day and ends on the day
-- before the same date N years later.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE, `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `the earlier day` `to` `the later day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the later day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the earlier day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the month` EQUALS 2 AND `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29
           IF `the month` EQUALS 2 THEN 28
           IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month count` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` PLUS ((`the month count` MINUS (`the month count` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS `months after` (`n` TIMES 12) `the day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `a` `and` `b` MEANS IF `a` `is on or before` `b` THEN `b` ELSE `a`

§§ `Scope -- the injuries this encoding covers`

-- Regulation cl 8: Part 4 (pre-injury average weekly earnings) "applies only to injuries received on or after 21 October
-- 2019"; earlier injuries fall under Part 3 and, before 2012, under the Schedule 6 transitional provisions (out of scope).
-- Schedule 6 Pt 19H cl 25 and 26, Pt 19I cl 14 and 15, Pt 19L cl 4 and 5: the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments do not apply
-- "to or in respect of an injury received by a police officer, paramedic or firefighter" or "by a coal miner" ("a
-- worker employed in or about a mine"); the law as it stood before them is not deposited.
DECLARE `Worker class` IS ONE OF
    `none of the classes Schedule 6 sets apart`
    `a police officer, paramedic or firefighter`
    `a coal miner`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the injury was received before 21 October 2019: Regulation Part 3 and the Schedule 6 transitional provisions apply, which this encoding does not cover`
    `the worker is a police officer, paramedic or firefighter: Schedule 6 keeps the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from the injury, and the earlier law is not deposited`
    `the worker is a coal miner: Schedule 6 keeps the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from the injury, and the earlier law is not deposited`
    `the s 66(2)(a) and (b) amounts for more than 10% and not more than 50% are formulas that are missing from the deposited text`
    `the death occurred before 21 October 2019, outside the window this encoding covers`

`the first day of Regulation Part 4` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 21 10 2019

GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE, `the class` IS A `Worker class`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the scope check` `the day of the injury` `the class` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the first day of Regulation Part 4` `is on or before` `the day of the injury`)
           THEN JUST `the injury was received before 21 October 2019: Regulation Part 3 and the Schedule 6 transitional provisions apply, which this encoding does not cover`
           IF `the class` EQUALS `a police officer, paramedic or firefighter`
           THEN JUST `the worker is a police officer, paramedic or firefighter: Schedule 6 keeps the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from the injury, and the earlier law is not deposited`
           IF `the class` EQUALS `a coal miner`
           THEN JUST `the worker is a coal miner: Schedule 6 keeps the 2012, 2015 and 2018 amendments from the injury, and the earlier law is not deposited`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- For the death benefits the window is the same date, applied to the death: s 25(4) takes the lump sum "in force at the
-- date of death", and Schedule 6 Pt 19I cl 14(2) and 15(1A) apply the 2015 amendments of ss 25 and 26 to police officers,
-- paramedics, firefighters and coal miners too, so no class is set apart.
GIVEN `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Why not covered`
`the death scope check` `the day of the death` MEANS
    IF `the first day of Regulation Part 4` `is on or before` `the day of the death`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the death occurred before 21 October 2019, outside the window this encoding covers`

§§ `Divisions 6, 6A, 6B -- the amounts and their indexation`

-- The indexed amounts used here, with the figure each deposited text states and the provision that varies it:
--   s 34(1): "The maximum weekly compensation amount is $1,838.70" -- an adjustable amount (s 79(a), base index 240.5,
--     s 79(a1)), varied each 1 April and 1 October (s 80) and declared by order (s 82).
--   s 38(3)(b): "at least $155 per week" -- varied each financial year under s 82B and declared by order (s 82B(2)).
--   s 38A(1): "$788.32" -- varied each 1 April and 1 October under s 82BA and declared by order (s 82BA(3)).
--   s 25(1)(a): "the amount of $750,000 (the lump sum death benefit)" and s 25(1)(b): "$66.60 per week" -- adjustable
--     amounts under Division 6 (s 79(a)); s 25(4): the lump sum is the amount "in force at the date of death".
-- The formulas of ss 80, 82A, 82B, 82BA and 82F were lost in conversion: only "calculated as follows--" or "the
-- formula--" and the "where" clauses survive. The declared amount is therefore an input; nothing here recomputes it.
DECLARE `Indexed amount` IS ONE OF
    `the maximum weekly compensation amount (s 34(1))`
    `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount`
    `the s 38A amount for a worker with highest needs`
    `the lump sum death benefit (s 25(1)(a))`
    `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 25(1)(b))`

GIVEN `the amount` IS AN `Indexed amount`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the figure in the deposited text for` `the amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amount`
    WHEN `the maximum weekly compensation amount (s 34(1))` THEN 1838.70
    WHEN `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount` THEN 155
    WHEN `the s 38A amount for a worker with highest needs` THEN 788.32
    WHEN `the lump sum death benefit (s 25(1)(a))` THEN 750000
    WHEN `the weekly payment for each dependent child (s 25(1)(b))` THEN 66.60

-- The current amount, if the person knows the declared figure; otherwise the figure in the deposited text.
GIVEN `the declared amount, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER, `the amount` IS AN `Indexed amount`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount that applies` `the declared amount, if known` `the amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the declared amount, if known`
    WHEN JUST `x` THEN `x`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the figure in the deposited text for` `the amount`

-- Regulation cl 8AB: "For the purposes of clause 2(4) of Schedule 3 to the 1987 Act, the amount of $155 is prescribed as
-- the minimum amount applicable to a worker." It is a figure of the Regulation, not one of the amounts s 82B varies
-- ("the amount of $155 specified in sections 38, 40 and 41"), so it is used as stated.
`the PIAWE minimum amount (Regulation cl 8AB)` MEANS 155

-- s 26: "reasonable funeral expenses not exceeding $15,000 or such other amount as may be prescribed by the
-- regulations". The deposited Regulation prescribes no other amount, and s 26 is not an adjustable amount under s 79.
`the funeral expenses maximum (s 26)` MEANS 15000

-- s 82A(1): the weekly payment "is to be varied on each review date" (1 April and 1 October) "by varying the amount of the
-- worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings ... in accordance with the formula" (lost in conversion); s 82A(4): the
-- Authority declares "the number that equates to the factor". s 82C(a): if the variation would reduce the amount, "the
-- variation is deemed not to have taken effect". s 82C(b) (a later increase counts only beyond an earlier reduction
-- not yet set off) needs the history of factors and is not applied: see NOTES.md.
GIVEN `the earnings as last varied` IS A NUMBER, `the declared factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earnings varied on the review date` `the earnings as last varied` `the declared factor` MEANS
    IF `the declared factor` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN `the earnings as last varied` TIMES `the declared factor`
    ELSE `the earnings as last varied`

§§ `Schedule 3 -- earnings and work capacity`

-- Sch 3 cl 2(1): pre-injury average weekly earnings means "the weekly average of the gross pre-injury earnings received by
-- the worker for work in any employment in which the worker was engaged at the time of the injury"; cl 2(2): only
-- earnings for work in "the period of 52 weeks ending immediately before the date of the injury (the relevant earning
-- period)", which the Regulation (Part 4 Division 2, cll 8A-8EA) may adjust -- the adjusted number of weeks is an INPUT.
-- cl 2(4) with Regulation cl 8AB: if the amount is less than $155, it "is taken to be that minimum amount".
GIVEN `the gross earnings in the relevant earning period` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks in the relevant earning period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the gross earnings in the relevant earning period` `the weeks in the relevant earning period` MEANS
    max (`the gross earnings in the relevant earning period` DIVIDED BY `the weeks in the relevant earning period`) `the PIAWE minimum amount (Regulation cl 8AB)`

-- Sch 3 cl 8: current weekly earnings "means whichever of the following is the greater amount -- (a) the worker's actual
-- gross earnings in respect of that week, (b) the weekly amount that the worker is able to earn in suitable employment".
-- Suitable employment (s 32A) is a judgment on the worker's circumstances "regardless of" whether the work is available:
-- the amount the worker is able to earn in it is a FACT.
GIVEN `the actual gross earnings for the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly amount the worker is able to earn in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the current weekly earnings` `the actual gross earnings for the week` `the weekly amount the worker is able to earn in suitable employment` MEANS
    max `the actual gross earnings for the week` `the weekly amount the worker is able to earn in suitable employment`

-- Sch 3 cl 9: current work capacity -- "a present inability arising from the injury such that the worker is able to
-- return to the worker's pre-injury employment, or ... to work in suitable employment, but the weekly amount that the
-- worker has the capacity to earn ... is less than" before the injury; no current work capacity -- "not able to return to
-- work, either in the worker's pre-injury employment or in suitable employment". Which one is a FACT here. A worker with
-- neither has no incapacity for work, and s 33 gives no weekly payment.
DECLARE `Work capacity` IS ONE OF
    `no current work capacity`
    `current work capacity`
    `no incapacity for work`

§§ `32A -- workers with high needs and highest needs`

-- s 32A(1): "worker with high needs means a worker whose injury has resulted in permanent impairment and -- (a) the degree
-- of permanent impairment has been assessed for the purposes of Division 4 to be more than 20%, or (b) an assessment ...
-- is pending and has not been made because a medical assessor has declined to make the assessment on the basis that
-- maximum medical improvement has not been reached ..., or (c) the insurer is satisfied that the degree of permanent
-- impairment is likely to be more than 20%, and includes a worker with highest needs." Note: "Paragraph (b) no longer
-- applies once the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed." Worker with highest needs: the same with 30%.
DECLARE `Impairment facts` HAS
    `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                              IS A NUMBER  -- per cent, as assessed under s 65
    `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`        IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Impairment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the assessment is pending` `the facts` IF
        (NOT (`the facts`'s `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`))
    AND `the facts`'s `an assessment is pending because maximum medical improvement is not reached`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Impairment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a worker with highest needs` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
    AND (    (    `the facts`'s `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`
              AND `the facts`'s `the assessed degree of permanent impairment` GREATER THAN 30)
         OR  `the assessment is pending` `the facts`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 30%`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Impairment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a worker with high needs` `the facts` IF
        `is a worker with highest needs` `the facts`
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
         AND (    (    `the facts`'s `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`
                   AND `the facts`'s `the assessed degree of permanent impairment` GREATER THAN 20)
              OR  `the assessment is pending` `the facts`
              OR  `the facts`'s `the insurer is satisfied the degree is likely to be more than 20%`))

§§ `32A -- the entitlement periods`

-- s 32A(1): "first entitlement period ... means an aggregate period not exceeding 13 weeks (whether or not consecutive) in
-- respect of which a weekly payment has been paid or is payable"; "second entitlement period ... means an aggregate
-- period of 117 weeks (whether or not consecutive) after the expiry of the first entitlement period". So weeks 1-13,
-- weeks 14-130, and after week 130 (s 38); s 39 ends weekly payments after "an aggregate period of 260 weeks".
-- Weeks are counted 1, 2, 3 ... over the weeks in respect of which a weekly payment has been paid or is payable.
DECLARE `Entitlement period` IS ONE OF
    `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
    `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)`
    `after the second entitlement period (weeks 131 to 260)`
    `after 260 weeks`

GIVEN `the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`the entitlement period for week` `the week` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the week` AT MOST 13  THEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)`
           IF `the week` AT MOST 130 THEN `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)`
           IF `the week` AT MOST 260 THEN `after the second entitlement period (weeks 131 to 260)`
           OTHERWISE `after 260 weeks`

-- The last week of the period the given week is in: where the rate steps down (13), where s 38 decides whether payments
-- go on (130), and where s 39 stops them unless the impairment is more than 20% (260). After 260 there is no set end
-- (only s 52 and s 38(8) reassessment).
GIVEN `the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last week of the entitlement period for week` `the week` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the week` AT MOST 13  THEN 13
           IF `the week` AT MOST 130 THEN 130
           IF `the week` AT MOST 260 THEN 260
           OTHERWISE `the week`

§§ `38 -- weekly payments after the second entitlement period`

-- s 38(1): entitlement "ceases on the expiry of the second entitlement period unless the worker is entitled to
-- compensation after the second entitlement period under this section".
-- s 38(2): a worker "assessed by the insurer as having no current work capacity and likely to continue indefinitely to have
-- no current work capacity is entitled".
-- s 38(3): a worker (other than a worker with high needs) "assessed by the insurer as having current work capacity is
-- entitled ... only if -- (a) the worker has applied to the insurer in writing (in the form approved by the Authority) no
-- earlier than 52 weeks before the end of the second entitlement period ..., and (b) the worker has returned to work ...
-- for a period of not less than 15 hours per week and is in receipt of current weekly earnings (or current weekly earnings
-- together with a deductible amount) of at least $155 per week, and (c) the worker is assessed by the insurer as being,
-- and as likely to continue indefinitely to be, incapable of undertaking further additional employment or work that would
-- increase the worker's current weekly earnings."
-- s 38(3A): a worker with high needs assessed as having current work capacity is entitled "only if the worker has applied
-- to the insurer in writing ... no earlier than 52 weeks before the end of the second entitlement period".
-- The insurer's assessments are judgments handed to the insurer: FACTS. "deductible amount" is not defined anywhere in
-- the deposited texts (finding): the earnings figure is asked as the worker's current weekly earnings with any such amount.
DECLARE `After week 130 facts` HAS
    `the insurer assessed no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer assessed current work capacity`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker applied in writing in the approved form`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of the second entitlement period left when the worker applied`             IS A NUMBER
    `hours a week the worker has returned to work`                                    IS A NUMBER
    `current weekly earnings, with any deductible amount`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the insurer assessed the worker as indefinitely unable to earn more`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 38(3)(a), (3A): "no earlier than 52 weeks before the end of the second entitlement period". The text sets no latest
-- day (finding): an application after the end also meets the words.
GIVEN `weeks left` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is no earlier than 52 weeks before the end` `weeks left` IF `weeks left` AT MOST 52

DECLARE `After week 130 answer` IS ONE OF
    `entitled after week 130: no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely (s 38(2))`
    `entitled after week 130: a worker with high needs with current work capacity who applied in time (s 38(3A))`
    `entitled after week 130: the s 38(3) conditions are met`
    `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` HAS `the condition not met` IS A STRING

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `After week 130 facts`
      `a worker with high needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `After week 130 answer`
`the s 38 entitlement` `the facts` `a worker with high needs` `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the facts`'s `the insurer assessed no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely`
           THEN `entitled after week 130: no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely (s 38(2))`
           IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the insurer assessed current work capacity`)
           THEN `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` "s 38(2) or (3): the insurer has assessed neither no current work capacity likely to continue indefinitely, nor current work capacity"
           IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the worker applied in writing in the approved form` AND `the application is no earlier than 52 weeks before the end` (`the facts`'s `weeks of the second entitlement period left when the worker applied`))
           THEN `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` "s 38(3)(a) or (3A): no written application in the approved form made no earlier than 52 weeks before the end of the second entitlement period"
           IF `a worker with high needs`
           THEN `entitled after week 130: a worker with high needs with current work capacity who applied in time (s 38(3A))`
           IF NOT (`the facts`'s `hours a week the worker has returned to work` AT LEAST 15 AND `the facts`'s `current weekly earnings, with any deductible amount` AT LEAST `the s 38(3)(b) earnings amount`)
           THEN `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` "s 38(3)(b): not returned to work for at least 15 hours a week with current weekly earnings of at least the s 38(3)(b) amount"
           IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the insurer assessed the worker as indefinitely unable to earn more`)
           THEN `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` "s 38(3)(c): the insurer has not assessed the worker as indefinitely incapable of further work that would increase the worker's current weekly earnings"
           OTHERWISE `entitled after week 130: the s 38(3) conditions are met`

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `After week 130 answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled after week 130` `the answer` IS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `not entitled after week 130 (s 38(1))` `why` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `39 -- no weekly payments after 260 weeks, unless the impairment is more than 20%`

-- s 39(1): "a worker has no entitlement to weekly payments ... after an aggregate period of 260 weeks"; s 39(2): "This
-- section does not apply to an injured worker whose injury results in permanent impairment if the degree of permanent
-- impairment resulting from the injury is more than 20%", assessed as provided by s 65 (s 39(3)). A pending assessment or
-- the insurer's view (which count for "high needs") does not count here: the degree must be assessed.
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Impairment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the injury has resulted in permanent impairment`
    AND `the facts`'s `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`
    AND `the facts`'s `the assessed degree of permanent impairment` GREATER THAN 20

§§ `52 -- the retiring age`

-- s 52(1): "retiring age ... means the age at which the person would ... be eligible to receive an age pension under the
-- Social Security Act 1991 of the Commonwealth" -- an INPUT (the day the person reaches it; Social Security Act 1991
-- s 23(5A)-(5D), deposited at subjects/au/social-security-act-1991/).
-- s 52(2)(a): injured before reaching the retiring age -- no weekly payment for incapacity "occurring after the first
-- anniversary of the date on which that person reaches the retiring age"; (b) injured on or after it -- none for
-- incapacity "occurring more than 12 months after the first occasion of incapacity for work resulting from the injury".
-- s 52(3): "notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Division". The answer is the last day of incapacity for which
-- a weekly payment may be made.
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day the worker reaches the retiring age` IS A DATE
      `the day of the first incapacity for work` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52` `the day of the injury` `the day the worker reaches the retiring age` `the day of the first incapacity for work` MEANS
    IF `the day of the injury` `is on or before` (`days after` (-1) `the day the worker reaches the retiring age`)
    THEN `years after` 1 `the day the worker reaches the retiring age`
    ELSE `months after` 12 `the day of the first incapacity for work`

§§ `33-38A -- the weekly payment`

-- s 33: "If total or partial incapacity for work results from an injury, the compensation payable ... shall include a
-- weekly payment during the incapacity."
-- s 34(1AA): "A weekly payment of compensation under this Subdivision is not to exceed the maximum weekly compensation
-- amount."
-- s 36(1): no current work capacity, first entitlement period: "95% of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings";
-- s 36(2): current work capacity: "the lesser of ... (a) 95% of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings, less the
-- worker's current weekly earnings, (b) the maximum weekly compensation amount, less the worker's current weekly earnings".
-- s 37(1): no current work capacity, second entitlement period: 80%; s 37(2): current work capacity "and has returned to
-- work for not less than 15 hours per week": the lesser of 95% less current weekly earnings and the maximum less current
-- weekly earnings; s 37(3): less than 15 hours (or not returned): the same with 80%.
-- s 38(6): after the second entitlement period, no current work capacity: 80%; s 38(7): current work capacity: the lesser
-- of 80% less current weekly earnings and the maximum less current weekly earnings.
-- Sch 3 cl 2(4) with Regulation cl 8AB: pre-injury average weekly earnings below $155 are taken to be $155.
-- READING: an amount below nil is nil (the Act does not say so; a weekly payment cannot be negative).
-- s 38A(1): "If the determination of the amount of weekly payments of compensation payable to a worker with highest needs
-- in accordance with this Subdivision results in an amount that is less than $788.32, the amount is to be treated as
-- $788.32" -- read literally, also where the amount worked out is nil (finding).
DECLARE `Weekly facts` HAS
    `which week of weekly payments this is`                              IS A NUMBER  -- 1 for the first week paid or payable
    `the work capacity`                                                  IS A `Work capacity`
    `the pre-injury average weekly earnings`                             IS A NUMBER  -- as varied under s 82A
    `the current weekly earnings`                                        IS A NUMBER  -- Sch 3 cl 8
    `hours a week the worker has returned to work`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the maximum weekly compensation amount`                             IS A NUMBER
    `the s 38A amount`                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `a worker with highest needs`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker is entitled after the second entitlement period under s 38` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks under s 39(2)`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the incapacity`                                          IS A DATE
    `the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52`            IS A DATE

DECLARE `Why no weekly payment` IS ONE OF
    `the incapacity falls after the last day s 52 allows, because of the retiring age`
    `there is no incapacity for work (s 33)`
    `260 weeks of weekly payments have been paid or are payable, and the impairment is not assessed at more than 20% (s 39)`
    `the second entitlement period has ended and s 38 does not continue the payments (s 38(1))`

DECLARE `Weekly payment` IS ONE OF
    `a weekly payment of` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `no weekly payment` HAS `because` IS A `Why no weekly payment`
    `the weekly payment is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

-- The percentage of pre-injury average weekly earnings the section uses.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the percentage of pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entitlement period for week` (`the facts`'s `which week of weekly payments this is`)
    WHEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)` THEN 0.95
    WHEN `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)` THEN
        IF      `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `current work capacity`
            AND `the facts`'s `hours a week the worker has returned to work` AT LEAST 15
        THEN 0.95
        ELSE 0.80
    OTHERWISE 0.80

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A STRING
`the section that sets the rate` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the entitlement period for week` (`the facts`'s `which week of weekly payments this is`)
    WHEN `the first entitlement period (weeks 1 to 13)` THEN
        IF `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `no current work capacity` THEN "s 36(1)" ELSE "s 36(2)"
    WHEN `the second entitlement period (weeks 14 to 130)` THEN
        IF `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `no current work capacity`
        THEN "s 37(1)"
        ELSE IF `the facts`'s `hours a week the worker has returned to work` AT LEAST 15 THEN "s 37(2)" ELSE "s 37(3)"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `no current work capacity` THEN "s 38(6)" ELSE "s 38(7)"

-- The amount the section works out, capped by s 34(1AA), before s 38A.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the section works out` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `no current work capacity`
    THEN min `the percentage amount` (`the facts`'s `the maximum weekly compensation amount`)
    ELSE max 0 (min (`the percentage amount` MINUS `the facts`'s `the current weekly earnings`) (`the facts`'s `the maximum weekly compensation amount` MINUS `the facts`'s `the current weekly earnings`))
    WHERE
        `the percentage amount` MEANS (max (`the facts`'s `the pre-injury average weekly earnings`) `the PIAWE minimum amount (Regulation cl 8AB)`) TIMES `the percentage of pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the facts`

-- s 38A, then s 34(1AA) again (the floor never exceeds the maximum on the deposited figures; the cap is kept in case a
-- declared floor does).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly payment amount` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `a worker with highest needs` AND `the amount the section works out` `the facts` LESS THAN `the facts`'s `the s 38A amount`
    THEN min (`the facts`'s `the s 38A amount`) (`the facts`'s `the maximum weekly compensation amount`)
    ELSE `the amount the section works out` `the facts`

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`, `the facts` IS A `Weekly facts`
GIVETH A `Weekly payment`
`the weekly payment` `the scope` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the weekly payment is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        BRANCH IF NOT ((`the facts`'s `the day of the incapacity`) `is on or before` (`the facts`'s `the last day weekly payments may be made for under s 52`))
               THEN `no weekly payment` `the incapacity falls after the last day s 52 allows, because of the retiring age`
               IF `the facts`'s `the work capacity` EQUALS `no incapacity for work`
               THEN `no weekly payment` `there is no incapacity for work (s 33)`
               IF `the facts`'s `which week of weekly payments this is` GREATER THAN 260 AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `weekly payments may continue after 260 weeks under s 39(2)`))
               THEN `no weekly payment` `260 weeks of weekly payments have been paid or are payable, and the impairment is not assessed at more than 20% (s 39)`
               IF `the facts`'s `which week of weekly payments this is` GREATER THAN 130 AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `the worker is entitled after the second entitlement period under s 38`))
               THEN `no weekly payment` `the second entitlement period has ended and s 38 does not continue the payments (s 38(1))`
               IF `the facts`'s `a worker with highest needs` AND `the amount the section works out` `the facts` LESS THAN `the facts`'s `the s 38A amount`
               THEN `a weekly payment of` (`the weekly payment amount` `the facts`) (CONCAT (`the section that sets the rate` `the facts`), ", raised to the s 38A amount")
               OTHERWISE `a weekly payment of` (`the weekly payment amount` `the facts`) (`the section that sets the rate` `the facts`)

GIVEN `the payment` IS A `Weekly payment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of` `the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a weekly payment of` `amount` `under` THEN `amount`
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `59A -- how long medical expenses are paid`

-- s 59A(1): compensation under Division 3 "is not payable ... in respect of any treatment, service or assistance given or
-- provided after the expiry of the compensation period". s 59A(2): the compensation period is "(a) if the injury has
-- resulted in a degree of permanent impairment assessed as provided by section 65 to be 10% or less, or the degree of
-- permanent impairment has not been assessed ..., the period of 2 years commencing on -- (i) the day on which the claim
-- for compensation in respect of the injury was first made (if weekly payments of compensation are not or have not been
-- paid or payable to the worker), or (ii) the day on which weekly payments of compensation cease to be payable to the
-- worker (if weekly payments of compensation are or have been paid or payable ...), or (b) ... more than 10% but not
-- more than 20%, the period of 5 years commencing on" the same days.
-- s 59A(3): if weekly payments become payable again, medical compensation is again payable "but only in respect of any
-- treatment, service or assistance given or provided during a period in respect of which weekly payments are payable".
-- s 59A(5): "This section does not apply to a worker with high needs". s 59A(6): nor to "(a) the provision of crutches,
-- artificial members, eyes or teeth and other artificial aids or spectacles (including hearing aids and hearing aid
-- batteries), (b) the modification of a worker's home or vehicle, (c) secondary surgery". s 59A(7): surgery is secondary
-- surgery if "(a) the surgery is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects a part of the body affected by the
-- earlier surgery, and (b) the surgery is approved by the insurer within 2 years after the earlier surgery was approved
-- (or is approved later than that pursuant to the determination of a dispute that arose within that 2 years)".
DECLARE `Treatment kind` IS ONE OF
    `crutches, artificial members, eyes or teeth, or other artificial aids or spectacles (including hearing aids and batteries)`
    `the modification of the worker's home or vehicle`
    `surgery`
    `other treatment, service or assistance`

DECLARE `Medical facts` HAS
    `the kind of treatment`                                                      IS A `Treatment kind`
    `the surgery is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects the same part of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer approved it within 2 years after approving the earlier surgery, or later on a dispute raised within them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a worker with high needs`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assessed degree of permanent impairment`                                IS A NUMBER
    `weekly payments are or have been paid or payable`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly payments are still payable`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the claim was first made`                                           IS A DATE
    `the day weekly payments ceased to be payable`                               IS A DATE

DECLARE `Medical compensation period` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
    `no time limit for this kind of treatment (s 59A(6))`
    `the compensation period has not begun: it will run for this many years from the day weekly payments cease (s 59A(2))` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER
    `payable for treatment given up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE, `years` IS A NUMBER
    `the medical compensation period is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Medical facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment is outside s 59A` `the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the kind of treatment`
    WHEN `crutches, artificial members, eyes or teeth, or other artificial aids or spectacles (including hearing aids and batteries)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the modification of the worker's home or vehicle` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `surgery` THEN
            `the facts`'s `the surgery is directly consequential on earlier surgery and affects the same part of the body`
        AND `the facts`'s `the insurer approved it within 2 years after approving the earlier surgery, or later on a dispute raised within them`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Medical facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years of the compensation period` `the facts` MEANS
    IF      `the facts`'s `the degree of permanent impairment has been assessed`
        AND `the facts`'s `the assessed degree of permanent impairment` GREATER THAN 10
    THEN 5
    ELSE 2

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Medical facts`
GIVETH A `Medical compensation period`
`the medical compensation period` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the facts`'s `a worker with high needs`
           THEN `no time limit: s 59A does not apply to a worker with high needs (s 59A(5))`
           IF `the treatment is outside s 59A` `the facts`
           THEN `no time limit for this kind of treatment (s 59A(6))`
           IF `the facts`'s `weekly payments are or have been paid or payable` AND `the facts`'s `weekly payments are still payable`
           THEN `the compensation period has not begun: it will run for this many years from the day weekly payments cease (s 59A(2))` (`the years of the compensation period` `the facts`)
           IF `the facts`'s `weekly payments are or have been paid or payable`
           THEN `payable for treatment given up to and including` (`days after` (-1) (`years after` (`the years of the compensation period` `the facts`) (`the facts`'s `the day weekly payments ceased to be payable`))) (`the years of the compensation period` `the facts`)
           OTHERWISE `payable for treatment given up to and including` (`days after` (-1) (`years after` (`the years of the compensation period` `the facts`) (`the facts`'s `the day the claim was first made`))) (`the years of the compensation period` `the facts`)

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`, `the facts` IS A `Medical facts`
GIVETH A `Medical compensation period`
`the medical compensation period, within scope` `the scope` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the medical compensation period is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the medical compensation period` `the facts`

-- Whether treatment given on a day falls inside: within the period, or (s 59A(3)) during a period for which weekly payments
-- are payable again.
DECLARE `Treatment day answer` IS ONE OF
    `compensation is payable for treatment on that day`
    `compensation is payable for treatment on that day, as weekly payments are payable again (s 59A(3))`
    `not payable: the treatment is after the compensation period ended (s 59A(1))`
    `treatment on that day is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the period` IS A `Medical compensation period`
      `the day of the treatment` IS A DATE
      `weekly payments are payable for that day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Treatment day answer`
`medical compensation for treatment on the day` `the period` `the day of the treatment` `weekly payments are payable for that day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period`
    WHEN `payable for treatment given up to and including` `the last day` `years` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the day of the treatment` `is on or before` `the last day`
               THEN `compensation is payable for treatment on that day`
               IF `weekly payments are payable for that day`
               THEN `compensation is payable for treatment on that day, as weekly payments are payable again (s 59A(3))`
               OTHERWISE `not payable: the treatment is after the compensation period ended (s 59A(1))`
    WHEN `the medical compensation period is not covered` `why` THEN `treatment on that day is not covered` `why`
    OTHERWISE `compensation is payable for treatment on that day`

§§ `66 -- permanent impairment compensation`

-- s 66(1): "A worker who receives an injury that results in a degree of permanent impairment greater than 10% is entitled
-- to receive from the worker's employer compensation for that permanent impairment". (1A): "Only one claim can be made".
-- s 66(2): "(a) if the degree of permanent impairment is greater than 10% but not greater than 30%, the amount ... is to be
-- calculated as follows--" and "(b) ... greater than 30% but not greater than 50%, ... as follows--": the formulas were
-- lost when the corpus converted the text, and only "where D is the number derived by expressing the degree of permanent
-- impairment as D%" survives. NOT COVERED (finding 1). (c) to (h) are stated amounts: more than 50% to 55%: $242,010;
-- to 60%: $309,020; to 65%: $376,030; to 70%: $443,030; to 74%: $510,040; more than 74%: $577,050. Each is a "variable
-- amount" (s 82E) varied each financial year under s 82F and declared by order (s 82F(3)): an INPUT, defaulting to the
-- stated figure. s 66(3): the amount "is to be calculated under this section as it was in force at the date the injury
-- was received" -- READING: the declared amount for the financial year in which the injury was received.
DECLARE `Section 66(2) paragraph` IS ONE OF
    `no paragraph: 10% or less`
    `paragraph (a): more than 10% and not more than 30%`
    `paragraph (b): more than 30% and not more than 50%`
    `paragraph (c): more than 50% and not more than 55%`
    `paragraph (d): more than 55% and not more than 60%`
    `paragraph (e): more than 60% and not more than 65%`
    `paragraph (f): more than 65% and not more than 70%`
    `paragraph (g): more than 70% and not more than 74%`
    `paragraph (h): more than 74%`

GIVEN `the degree` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Section 66(2) paragraph`
`the s 66(2) paragraph for` `the degree` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the degree` AT MOST 10 THEN `no paragraph: 10% or less`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 30 THEN `paragraph (a): more than 10% and not more than 30%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 50 THEN `paragraph (b): more than 30% and not more than 50%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 55 THEN `paragraph (c): more than 50% and not more than 55%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 60 THEN `paragraph (d): more than 55% and not more than 60%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 65 THEN `paragraph (e): more than 60% and not more than 65%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 70 THEN `paragraph (f): more than 65% and not more than 70%`
           IF `the degree` AT MOST 74 THEN `paragraph (g): more than 70% and not more than 74%`
           OTHERWISE `paragraph (h): more than 74%`

-- The stated amount of paragraphs (c) to (h); NOTHING where the paragraph states none.
GIVEN `the paragraph` IS A `Section 66(2) paragraph`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount stated in` `the paragraph` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the paragraph`
    WHEN `paragraph (c): more than 50% and not more than 55%` THEN JUST 242010
    WHEN `paragraph (d): more than 55% and not more than 60%` THEN JUST 309020
    WHEN `paragraph (e): more than 60% and not more than 65%` THEN JUST 376030
    WHEN `paragraph (f): more than 65% and not more than 70%` THEN JUST 443030
    WHEN `paragraph (g): more than 70% and not more than 74%` THEN JUST 510040
    WHEN `paragraph (h): more than 74%` THEN JUST 577050
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 66(2A): "To the extent to which the injury results in permanent impairment of the back, the amount ... calculated in
-- accordance with subsection (2) is to be increased by 5%." Its Example 2: 50% impairment, $175,000, two-thirds to the
-- back: two-thirds increased by 5% gives $122,500, and the total is $180,833.33. The share to the back is in per cent.
GIVEN `the s 66(2) amount` IS A NUMBER, `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount increased for the back` `the s 66(2) amount` `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` MEANS
    `the s 66(2) amount` PLUS (`the s 66(2) amount` TIMES `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES 0.05)

DECLARE `Permanent impairment answer` IS ONE OF
    `no permanent impairment compensation: the degree is 10% or less (s 66(1))`
    `no further claim: only one claim can be made for the impairment from an injury (s 66(1A))`
    `permanent impairment compensation of` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `under` IS A STRING
    `permanent impairment compensation is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`
      `the degree` IS A NUMBER
      `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` IS A NUMBER
      `a claim has already been made for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declared amount for the paragraph, if known` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Permanent impairment answer`
`the permanent impairment compensation` `the scope` `the degree` `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` `a claim has already been made for it` `the declared amount for the paragraph, if known` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `permanent impairment compensation is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        BRANCH IF `the degree` AT MOST 10
               THEN `no permanent impairment compensation: the degree is 10% or less (s 66(1))`
               IF `a claim has already been made for it`
               THEN `no further claim: only one claim can be made for the impairment from an injury (s 66(1A))`
               OTHERWISE
                   CONSIDER `the amount stated in` (`the s 66(2) paragraph for` `the degree`)
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN `permanent impairment compensation is not covered` `the s 66(2)(a) and (b) amounts for more than 10% and not more than 50% are formulas that are missing from the deposited text`
                   WHEN JUST `the stated amount` THEN
                       `permanent impairment compensation of`
                           (`the amount increased for the back` (`the amount that applies to the paragraph` `the stated amount`) `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back`)
                           (IF `the per cent of the impairment that is of the back` GREATER THAN 0 THEN "s 66(2), increased under s 66(2A)" ELSE "s 66(2)")
    WHERE
        `the amount that applies to the paragraph` `the stated amount` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the declared amount for the paragraph, if known`
            WHEN JUST `x` THEN `x`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the stated amount`

§§ `25, 26 -- compensation on death`

-- s 25(1): "If death results from an injury, the amount of compensation payable by the employer ... shall be -- (a) the
-- amount of $750,000 (the lump sum death benefit), which is to be apportioned among any dependants who are wholly or
-- partly dependent for support on the worker or (if there are no such dependants) paid to the worker's legal personal
-- representative". s 29(1A): not apportioned "if a deceased worker leaves only one dependant"; s 29(1B): with 2 or more,
-- "the whole lump sum death benefit is to be apportioned among those dependants". s 25(3): weekly payments and other
-- compensation are not deducted. s 25(4): the amount "in force at the date of death".
DECLARE `Who receives the lump sum` IS ONE OF
    `the one dependant, without apportionment (s 29(1A))`
    `the dependants, apportioned among them (s 29(1), (1B))`
    `the worker's legal personal representative, as there are no dependants (s 25(1)(a))`

DECLARE `Lump sum death benefit` HAS
    `the amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `paid to`     IS A `Who receives the lump sum`

GIVEN `the lump sum in force at the date of death` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Lump sum death benefit`
`the lump sum death benefit` `the lump sum in force at the date of death` `the number of dependants` MEANS
    `Lump sum death benefit` WITH
        `the amount` IS `the lump sum in force at the date of death`
        `paid to`    IS
            BRANCH IF `the number of dependants` EQUALS 0 THEN `the worker's legal personal representative, as there are no dependants (s 25(1)(a))`
                   IF `the number of dependants` EQUALS 1 THEN `the one dependant, without apportionment (s 29(1A))`
                   OTHERWISE `the dependants, apportioned among them (s 29(1), (1B))`

-- s 25(1)(b): "in addition, an amount of $66.60 per week in respect of -- (i) each dependent child of the worker under the
-- age of 16 years, and (ii) each dependent child of the worker being a student over the age of 16 years but under the
-- age of 21 years". s 25(2): the payments continue "(a) ... until the child dies or reaches the age of 16 years ..., or
-- (b) in the case of a dependent child who is a student at the time of the worker's death or after reaching the age of
-- 16 years -- until the child dies, reaches the age of 21 years or ceases to be a student". s 25(5): "dependent child of
-- the worker means a child [or stepchild, or a person to whom the worker stood in the place of a parent] who was wholly
-- or partly dependent for support on the worker"; "student means a person receiving full-time education at a school,
-- college or university". READINGS: "over the age of 16" includes a child of 16; a child under 16 is paid whether or not
-- a student (s 25(1)(b)(i)), although s 25(2)(b) read alone would stop the payment for a student under 16 who leaves
-- full-time education (finding).
GIVEN `the child was wholly or partly dependent for support on the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child's age in whole years` IS A NUMBER
      `the child is in full-time education at a school, college or university` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a weekly payment is payable for the child` `the child was wholly or partly dependent for support on the worker` `the child's age in whole years` `the child is in full-time education at a school, college or university` IF
        `the child was wholly or partly dependent for support on the worker`
    AND (    `the child's age in whole years` LESS THAN 16
         OR  (`the child is in full-time education at a school, college or university` AND `the child's age in whole years` LESS THAN 21))

-- s 26: "the employer must pay additional compensation equal to reasonable funeral expenses not exceeding $15,000".
-- Whether an expense is reasonable is a FACT.
GIVEN `the reasonable funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the funeral expenses payable` `the reasonable funeral expenses` MEANS
    min `the reasonable funeral expenses` `the funeral expenses maximum (s 26)`

-- The death answers, with the window applied.
DECLARE `Death benefit answer` IS ONE OF
    `the lump sum death benefit is` HAS `the benefit` IS A `Lump sum death benefit`
    `the death benefit is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

DECLARE `Amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `an amount of` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the amount is not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`, `the lump sum in force at the date of death` IS A NUMBER, `the number of dependants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Death benefit answer`
`the death benefit` `the scope` `the lump sum in force at the date of death` `the number of dependants` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the death benefit is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the lump sum death benefit is` (`the lump sum death benefit` `the lump sum in force at the date of death` `the number of dependants`)

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`
      `the weekly amount for a dependent child` IS A NUMBER
      `the child qualifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the weekly payment for the child` `the scope` `the weekly amount for a dependent child` `the child qualifies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the amount is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `an amount of` (IF `the child qualifies` THEN `the weekly amount for a dependent child` ELSE 0)

GIVEN `the scope` IS A MAYBE `Why not covered`, `the reasonable funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the funeral expenses answer` `the scope` `the reasonable funeral expenses` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the scope`
    WHEN JUST `why` THEN `the amount is not covered` `why`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `an amount of` (`the funeral expenses payable` `the reasonable funeral expenses`)

§§ `1998 Act s 254 -- notice of injury to the employer`

-- s 254(1): "Neither compensation nor work injury damages are recoverable by an injured worker unless notice of the injury
-- is given to the employer as soon as possible after the injury happened and before the worker has voluntarily left the
-- employment in which the worker was at the time of the injury." s 254(2): the failure "is not a bar ... if in
-- proceedings to recover the compensation ... it is found that there are special circumstances". s 254(3)-(4) list them.
-- The finding is the Commission's: asked as a FACT ("special circumstances are found").
DECLARE `Special circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `no special circumstance`
    `the employer was not prejudiced by the failure, defect or inaccuracy (s 254(3)(a))`
    `ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause (s 254(3)(b))`
    `the employer knew of the injury at or about the time it happened (s 254(3)(c))`
    `the employer reported the injury to the Nominal Insurer (s 254(3)(d))`
    `the employer contravened s 231 (s 254(3)(e), (4)(a))`
    `the injury was treated in a first aid room at the place of work (s 254(3)(f), (4)(c))`
    `the employer reported the injury to an inspector of mines or a WHS inspector (s 254(3)(g), (4)(b))`

DECLARE `Notice of injury answer` IS ONE OF
    `notice of injury is no bar: it was given as soon as possible and before the worker left the employment (s 254(1))`
    `the failure is no bar, if the special circumstance is found in proceedings (s 254(2))`
    `compensation is not recoverable: notice was not given as s 254(1) requires, and no special circumstance applies`

GIVEN `notice was given to the employer as soon as possible after the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given before the worker voluntarily left the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the special circumstance` IS A `Special circumstance`
GIVETH A `Notice of injury answer`
`the notice of injury position` `notice was given to the employer as soon as possible after the injury` `notice was given before the worker voluntarily left the employment` `the special circumstance` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `notice was given to the employer as soon as possible after the injury` AND `notice was given before the worker voluntarily left the employment`
           THEN `notice of injury is no bar: it was given as soon as possible and before the worker left the employment (s 254(1))`
           IF `the special circumstance` EQUALS `no special circumstance`
           THEN `compensation is not recoverable: notice was not given as s 254(1) requires, and no special circumstance applies`
           OTHERWISE `the failure is no bar, if the special circumstance is found in proceedings (s 254(2))`

§§ `1998 Act s 261 -- the time for making a claim`

-- s 261(1): "Compensation cannot be recovered unless a claim for the compensation has been made within 6 months after the
-- injury or accident happened or, in the case of death, within 6 months after the date of death." (2): a timely claim by
-- the worker carries over to a claim for the worker's death from that injury. (4): no bar "if it is found that the failure
-- was occasioned by ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause, and either -- (a) the claim is
-- made within 3 years after the injury ... or, in the case of death, within 3 years after the date of death, or (b) the
-- claim is not made within that 3 years but the claim is in respect of an injury resulting in the death or serious and
-- permanent disablement of a worker". (5): no bar "if the insurer concerned determines to accept the claim outside that
-- period. An insurer cannot determine to accept a claim made more than 3 years after the injury ... except with the
-- approval of the Authority." (6): if the worker "first becomes aware that he or she has received an injury after the
-- injury was received, the injury is ... taken to have been received when the worker first became so aware"; (7) the
-- same for a claimant's awareness that a death resulted from the injury. Findings and the insurer's and Authority's
-- decisions are FACTS.
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE, `the day the claimant first became aware of it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day time runs from under s 261(6), (7)` `the day it happened` `the day the claimant first became aware of it` MEANS
    `the later of` `the day it happened` `and` `the day the claimant first became aware of it`

DECLARE `Claim time facts` HAS
    `the claim is for compensation for a death`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day time runs from`                                                    IS A DATE  -- s 261(1), (6), (7)
    `the day the claim was made`                                                IS A DATE
    `the worker made a claim within time for the injury that caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 261(2)
    `the lateness is found to come from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the insurer has determined to accept the claim`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Authority approved the insurer's acceptance`                           IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Claim time answer` IS ONE OF
    `made in time: within 6 months (s 261(1))`
    `in time: the worker's own claim was made in time (s 261(2))`
    `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and made within 3 years (s 261(4)(a))`
    `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement (s 261(4)(b))`
    `late, but no bar: the insurer determined to accept it (s 261(5))`
    `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Claim time facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is made within 6 months` `the facts` IF
    (`the facts`'s `the day the claim was made`) `is on or before` (`months after` 6 (`the facts`'s `the day time runs from`))

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Claim time facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is made within 3 years` `the facts` IF
    (`the facts`'s `the day the claim was made`) `is on or before` (`years after` 3 (`the facts`'s `the day time runs from`))

-- s 261(5), second sentence: may the insurer determine to accept the late claim?
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Claim time facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may determine to accept the late claim` `the facts` IF
    `the claim is made within 3 years` `the facts` OR `the facts`'s `the Authority approved the insurer's acceptance`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Claim time facts`
GIVETH A `Claim time answer`
`the claim time position` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the claim is made within 6 months` `the facts`
           THEN `made in time: within 6 months (s 261(1))`
           IF `the facts`'s `the claim is for compensation for a death` AND `the facts`'s `the worker made a claim within time for the injury that caused the death`
           THEN `in time: the worker's own claim was made in time (s 261(2))`
           IF `the facts`'s `the lateness is found to come from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` AND `the claim is made within 3 years` `the facts`
           THEN `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and made within 3 years (s 261(4)(a))`
           IF `the facts`'s `the lateness is found to come from ignorance, mistake, absence from the State or other reasonable cause` AND `the facts`'s `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement`
           THEN `late, but no bar: reasonable cause, and the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement (s 261(4)(b))`
           IF `the facts`'s `the insurer has determined to accept the claim` AND `the insurer may determine to accept the late claim` `the facts`
           THEN `late, but no bar: the insurer determined to accept it (s 261(5))`
           OTHERWISE `late, and compensation cannot be recovered (s 261(1))`

§§ `Deadlines -- 1998 Act ss 264, 267, 268, 274, 48A; Regulation cl 35`

-- The position of a duty that must be done by a day.
DECLARE `Deadline answer` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `done late: the deadline was` HAS `the deadline` IS A DATE
    `not yet done, and the deadline has not passed: it is` HAS `the deadline` IS A DATE
    `missed: not done by the deadline` HAS `the deadline` IS A DATE
    `no such duty`

GIVEN `the due day` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`the deadline position` `the due day` `it has been done` `the day it was done` `the day in question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it has been done` AND (`the day it was done` `is on or before` `the due day`)
           THEN `done in time`
           IF `it has been done`
           THEN `done late: the deadline was` `the due day`
           IF `the day in question` `is on or before` `the due day`
           THEN `not yet done, and the deadline has not passed: it is` `the due day`
           OTHERWISE `missed: not done by the deadline` `the due day`

-- 1998 Act ss 267, 268: within 7 days of the initial notification the insurer must either start provisional weekly
-- payments or (with a reasonable excuse) give the worker written notice of the excuse; whichever it did is the one
-- measured, and if it did neither, the deadline is missed once the 7 days pass.
GIVEN `the day of the initial notification` IS A DATE
      `provisional weekly payments have started` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they started` IS A DATE
      `written notice of a reasonable excuse has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the excuse notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Deadline answer`
`the position under ss 267 and 268` `the day of the initial notification` `provisional weekly payments have started` `the day they started` `written notice of a reasonable excuse has been given` `the day the excuse notice was given` `the day in question` MEANS
    IF `provisional weekly payments have started`
    THEN `the deadline position` `the 7th day` TRUE `the day they started` `the day in question`
    ELSE `the deadline position` `the 7th day` `written notice of a reasonable excuse has been given` `the day the excuse notice was given` `the day in question`
    WHERE
        `the 7th day` MEANS `days after` `the days to start provisional weekly payments (1998 Act s 267(1))` `the day of the initial notification`

GIVEN `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Duty`
`the duty within 7 days of the initial notification` `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` MEANS
    IF `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines`
    THEN `the insurer's duty to give notice of a reasonable excuse within 7 days (1998 Act s 268)`
    ELSE `the insurer's duty to start provisional weekly payments within 7 days (1998 Act s 267)`

-- 1998 Act s 274(2), (4): provisional acceptance "for a period of up to 12 weeks", but not "if the insurer is already
-- making weekly payments on the basis of the provisional acceptance of liability under Division 1 when the claim for
-- weekly payments is made".
GIVEN `the weeks` IS A NUMBER, `provisional payments under Division 1 were being made when the claim was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurer may accept liability provisionally under s 274(2)` `the weeks` `provisional payments under Division 1 were being made when the claim was made` IF
        (NOT (`provisional payments under Division 1 were being made when the claim was made`))
    AND `the weeks` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the weeks` AT MOST `the most weeks of provisional acceptance (1998 Act ss 267(3), 274(2))`

-- 1998 Act s 44(2), (4) and s 264(1): no duty for a self-insurer.
GIVEN `the employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the hours to notify the insurer, if any` `the employer is a self-insurer` MEANS
    IF `the employer is a self-insurer` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST `the hours to notify the insurer (1998 Act s 44(2))`

GIVEN `the employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day the claim was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day to forward the claim by, if any` `the employer is a self-insurer` `the day the claim was received` MEANS
    IF `the employer is a self-insurer` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (`days after` `the days to forward a claim (1998 Act s 264(1))` `the day the claim was received`)

-- The days the Acts and the Regulation give.
`the hours to notify the insurer (1998 Act s 44(2))` MEANS 48
`the days to forward a claim (1998 Act s 264(1))` MEANS 7
`the days to give requested information (1998 Act s 264(2))` MEANS 7
`the days to start provisional weekly payments (1998 Act s 267(1))` MEANS 7
`the days to give notice of a reasonable excuse (1998 Act s 268)` MEANS 7
`the days to determine a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274(1))` MEANS 21
`the most weeks of provisional acceptance (1998 Act ss 267(3), 274(2))` MEANS 12
`the fewest days to the date in a s 48A notice` MEANS 14
`the most days to the date in a s 48A notice` MEANS 60
`the days of a s 48A suspension` MEANS 28
`the days to make the notification records available (Regulation cl 35(3))` MEANS 7
`the years to keep the notification records (Regulation cl 35(2))` MEANS 5
-- The last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period are 364 days: day 0 (their first day) to day 363 (the last day of
-- the period).
`the last day of the last 52 weeks, counted from their first day` MEANS 363
-- READING: "at least once every 2 years" (s 38(4)(b)) is counted as 730 days on the rule's clock; the date questions use
-- the same date 2 years later.
`the days in 2 years for s 38(4)(b)` MEANS 730

-- s 274(1): "Within 21 days after a claim for weekly payments is made the person on whom the claim is made must determine
-- the claim by -- (a) accepting liability and commencing weekly payments, or (b) disputing liability." (2): the insurer
-- "can accept liability for weekly payments on a provisional basis for a period of up to 12 weeks"; (3): that "operates
-- to extend the period within which the claim must be determined until the end of the period for which liability has been
-- accepted on a provisional basis". s 275(2) and s 276(1) extend it the same way for provisional payments under s 267.
-- READING: the end of a provisional period of w weeks is w weeks after the day it began.
GIVEN `the day the claim was made` IS A DATE
      `weeks of provisional acceptance` IS A NUMBER  -- 0 if none
      `the day the provisional acceptance began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day by which the claim for weekly payments must be determined` `the day the claim was made` `weeks of provisional acceptance` `the day the provisional acceptance began` MEANS
    IF `weeks of provisional acceptance` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the later of` (`days after` `the days to determine a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274(1))` `the day the claim was made`) `and` (`days after` (7 TIMES (min `weeks of provisional acceptance` `the most weeks of provisional acceptance (1998 Act ss 267(3), 274(2))`)) `the day the provisional acceptance began`)
    ELSE `days after` `the days to determine a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274(1))` `the day the claim was made`

-- s 48A(2)(b): the notice must state that payments "will be suspended from the date specified in the notice which must be
-- a date at least 14 days after notice is given but no more than 60 days after notice is given". (3): if the worker
-- fails to comply, "the insurer may suspend the payment of weekly payments ... for a period of 28 days after the date
-- specified". (6): if the worker does not comply "for the entire period" of suspension, the insurer "may terminate" by
-- written notice; (7): it may instead "cease and determine the entitlement" if, "within the last 12 months prior to the
-- giving of the notice", the worker had "(i) been issued 2 notices under subsection (2) without a subsequent suspension
-- ..., or (ii) had compensation in the form of weekly payments suspended once". (4)-(5): if the worker complies during
-- the suspension, the insurer "must ... resume the payment ... with effect from the date on which the worker complied",
-- and the payments for the suspended time are forfeited.
GIVEN `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE, `the date specified in the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date in the s 48A notice is allowed` `the day the notice was given` `the date specified in the notice` IF
        `days from` `the day the notice was given` `to` `the date specified in the notice` AT LEAST `the fewest days to the date in a s 48A notice`
    AND `days from` `the day the notice was given` `to` `the date specified in the notice` AT MOST `the most days to the date in a s 48A notice`

DECLARE `Section 48A answer` IS ONE OF
    `the insurer may not suspend: the notice does not meet s 48A(2)`
    `the insurer may not suspend: the worker complied by the date in the notice`
    `no suspension yet: the worker has until the date in the notice to comply` HAS `the date` IS A DATE
    `the insurer may suspend weekly payments for 28 days after the date in the notice, to` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the insurer must resume weekly payments from the day the worker complied, and the suspended payments are forfeited (s 48A(4), (5))` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `the insurer may terminate weekly payments by written notice stating the reasons (s 48A(6))`
    `the insurer may cease and determine the entitlement to weekly payments by written notice stating the reasons (s 48A(7))`

DECLARE `Section 48A facts` HAS
    `the day the notice was given`                                           IS A DATE
    `the date specified in the notice`                                       IS A DATE
    `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the worker complied`                                            IS A DATE
    `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day asked about`                                                    IS A DATE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Section 48A facts`
GIVETH A `Section 48A answer`
`what the insurer may do under s 48A` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences` AND `the date in the s 48A notice is allowed` (`the facts`'s `the day the notice was given`) (`the facts`'s `the date specified in the notice`))
           THEN `the insurer may not suspend: the notice does not meet s 48A(2)`
           IF `the facts`'s `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice` AND ((`the facts`'s `the day the worker complied`) `is on or before` (`the facts`'s `the date specified in the notice`))
           THEN `the insurer may not suspend: the worker complied by the date in the notice`
           IF (NOT (`the facts`'s `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice`)) AND ((`the facts`'s `the day asked about`) `is on or before` (`days after` (-1) (`the facts`'s `the date specified in the notice`)))
           THEN `no suspension yet: the worker has until the date in the notice to comply` (`the facts`'s `the date specified in the notice`)
           IF `the facts`'s `the worker has complied with the obligation in the notice` AND ((`the facts`'s `the day the worker complied`) `is on or before` `the end of the suspension`)
           THEN `the insurer must resume weekly payments from the day the worker complied, and the suspended payments are forfeited (s 48A(4), (5))` (`the facts`'s `the day the worker complied`)
           IF (`the facts`'s `the day asked about`) `is on or before` `the end of the suspension`
           THEN `the insurer may suspend weekly payments for 28 days after the date in the notice, to` `the end of the suspension`
           IF `the facts`'s `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension`
           THEN `the insurer may cease and determine the entitlement to weekly payments by written notice stating the reasons (s 48A(7))`
           OTHERWISE `the insurer may terminate weekly payments by written notice stating the reasons (s 48A(6))`
    WHERE
        `the end of the suspension` MEANS `days after` `the days of a s 48A suspension` (`the facts`'s `the date specified in the notice`)

-- 1998 Act s 49(1): if a worker "is able to return to work (whether on a full-time or part-time basis and whether or not
-- to his or her previous employment), the employer liable to pay compensation ... must at the request of the worker
-- provide suitable employment for the worker. Maximum penalty -- 50 penalty units." (3): not if "(a) it is not reasonably
-- practicable to provide employment ..., or (b) the worker voluntarily left the employment of that employer after the
-- injury happened ..., or (c) the employer terminated the worker's employment after the injury happened, other than for
-- the reason that the worker was not fit for employment as a result of the injury". Reasonable practicability is a FACT.
DECLARE `Suitable work facts` HAS
    `the worker is able to return to work`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker has asked the employer for suitable employment`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is not reasonably practicable to provide it`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker voluntarily left the employment after the injury`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer ended the employment after the injury, not for unfitness from the injury` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Suitable work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exception in s 49(3) applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `it is not reasonably practicable to provide it`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the worker voluntarily left the employment after the injury`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the employer ended the employment after the injury, not for unfitness from the injury`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Suitable work facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must provide suitable employment` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the worker is able to return to work`
    AND `the facts`'s `the worker has asked the employer for suitable employment`
    AND (NOT (`an exception in s 49(3) applies` `the facts`))

-- 1998 Act s 38(4)-(5) of the 1987 Act, for the insurer's work capacity assessments: (4) "An insurer must ... ensure
-- that a work capacity assessment of the worker is conducted -- (a) during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement
-- period, and (b) thereafter at least once every 2 years." (5) "An insurer is not to conduct a work capacity assessment of
-- a worker with highest needs unless the insurer thinks it appropriate to do so and the worker requests it."
DECLARE `Work capacity assessment answer` IS ONE OF
    `not to be conducted: a worker with highest needs who has not asked for one (s 38(5))`
    `may be conducted, if the insurer thinks it appropriate: a worker with highest needs who asked for one (s 38(5))`
    `conduct one during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period, between` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
    `conduct the next one by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

GIVEN `a worker with highest needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker has asked for an assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the second entitlement period` IS A DATE
      `an assessment has been done in the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the latest assessment` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Work capacity assessment answer`
`the work capacity assessments required` `a worker with highest needs` `the worker has asked for an assessment` `the last day of the second entitlement period` `an assessment has been done in the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period` `the day of the latest assessment` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a worker with highest needs` AND `the worker has asked for an assessment`
           THEN `may be conducted, if the insurer thinks it appropriate: a worker with highest needs who asked for one (s 38(5))`
           IF `a worker with highest needs`
           THEN `not to be conducted: a worker with highest needs who has not asked for one (s 38(5))`
           IF `an assessment has been done in the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period`
           THEN `conduct the next one by` (`years after` 2 `the day of the latest assessment`)
           OTHERWISE `conduct one during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period, between` (`days after` (0 MINUS `the last day of the last 52 weeks, counted from their first day`) `the last day of the second entitlement period`) `the last day of the second entitlement period`

-- Regulation cl 35(2): the employer "must make and keep for at least 5 years after the notification is given" the records
-- of the injury, of the notification and of any acknowledgment.
GIVEN `the day the notification was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the records must be kept until at least` `the day the notification was given` MEANS
    `years after` `the years to keep the notification records (Regulation cl 35(2))` `the day the notification was given`

§§ `What follows if a duty is missed`

-- Maximum penalties are those the deposited texts state; the penalty notice amounts are from Regulation Schedule 5
-- (cl 71), quoted here because they say what follows. The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes (Sentencing
-- Procedure) Act 1999, which is not deposited.
DECLARE `Duty` IS ONE OF
    `the employer's duty to notify the insurer within 48 hours (1998 Act s 44(2))`
    `the employer's duty to forward a claim within 7 days (1998 Act s 264(1))`
    `the employer's duty to give requested information within 7 days (1998 Act s 264(2))`
    `the employer's duty to provide suitable work (1998 Act s 49)`
    `the employer's duty to make notification records available within 7 days (Regulation cl 35(3))`
    `the insurer's duty to start provisional weekly payments within 7 days (1998 Act s 267)`
    `the insurer's duty to give notice of a reasonable excuse within 7 days (1998 Act s 268)`
    `the insurer's duty to determine a claim for weekly payments within 21 days (1998 Act ss 274, 283)`
    `the worker's duty to make reasonable efforts to return to work (1998 Act s 48)`

DECLARE `Consequence` HAS
    `maximum penalty in penalty units`  IS A NUMBER   -- 0 where the text creates no offence
    `penalty notice amount in dollars`  IS A NUMBER   -- 0 where Schedule 5 lists none
    `what else follows`                 IS A STRING

GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Duty`
GIVETH A `Consequence`
`the consequence of missing` `the duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the duty`
    WHEN `the employer's duty to notify the insurer within 48 hours (1998 Act s 44(2))` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 20
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 550
            `what else follows`                IS "Regulation cl 36: an offence (20 penalty units); penalty notice $550 (Schedule 5). Not for a self-insurer (s 44(4))."
    WHEN `the employer's duty to forward a claim within 7 days (1998 Act s 264(1))` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 1100
            `what else follows`                IS "s 264(1): an offence (50 penalty units), unless there was a reasonable excuse (s 264(4)); penalty notice $1,100 (Schedule 5). A self-insurer has no such duty."
    WHEN `the employer's duty to give requested information within 7 days (1998 Act s 264(2))` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 1100
            `what else follows`                IS "s 264(2): an offence (50 penalty units), unless there was a reasonable excuse (s 264(4)); penalty notice $1,100 (Schedule 5)."
    WHEN `the employer's duty to provide suitable work (1998 Act s 49)` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 0
            `what else follows`                IS "s 49(1): an offence (50 penalty units). Schedule 5 lists no penalty notice for it. No duty where s 49(3) applies."
    WHEN `the employer's duty to make notification records available within 7 days (Regulation cl 35(3))` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 20
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 0
            `what else follows`                IS "Regulation cl 35: an offence (20 penalty units). Schedule 5 lists no penalty notice for it."
    WHEN `the insurer's duty to start provisional weekly payments within 7 days (1998 Act s 267)` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 1100
            `what else follows`                IS "s 267(5): an offence (50 penalty units), unless the insurer has a reasonable excuse that the Workers Compensation Guidelines recognise (s 267(1), (2)), in which case s 268 applies; penalty notice $1,100 (Schedule 5)."
    WHEN `the insurer's duty to give notice of a reasonable excuse within 7 days (1998 Act s 268)` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 1100
            `what else follows`                IS "s 268: an offence (50 penalty units); penalty notice $1,100 (Schedule 5)."
    WHEN `the insurer's duty to determine a claim for weekly payments within 21 days (1998 Act ss 274, 283)` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 50
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 1100
            `what else follows`                IS "s 283(1): an offence (50 penalty units), unless the insurer has a reasonable excuse that the Workers Compensation Guidelines recognise (s 283(2)), which it must notify in writing as soon as practicable (s 283(3)); penalty notice $1,100 (Schedule 5)."
    WHEN `the worker's duty to make reasonable efforts to return to work (1998 Act s 48)` THEN
        `Consequence` WITH
            `maximum penalty in penalty units` IS 0
            `penalty notice amount in dollars` IS 0
            `what else follows`                IS "s 48A: no offence, but the insurer may give a notice and then suspend weekly payments for 28 days, and terminate them (or cease and determine the entitlement) if the worker does not comply."

§§ `Regulative rules -- the worker, the employer and the insurer`

DECLARE `WC party` IS ONE OF `the worker`, `the employer`, `the insurer`

DECLARE `Claim determination` IS ONE OF
    `accepting liability and commencing weekly payments`
    `disputing liability`
    `accepting liability provisionally for` HAS `weeks` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `WC act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the employer of the workplace injury`
    `notify the insurer of the workplace injury`
    `make a claim for compensation`
    `determine to accept the late claim`
    `forward the claim to the insurer`
    `give the insurer the information it requested`
    `commence provisional weekly payments`
    `give the worker notice of the s 269 matters`
    `give the worker written notice of the reasonable excuse`
    `determine the claim for weekly payments` HAS `how` IS A `Claim determination`
    `comply with the s 48 obligation in the notice`
    `suspend weekly payments`
    `resume weekly payments from the day the worker complied`
    `terminate weekly payments by written notice`
    `cease and determine the entitlement to weekly payments by written notice`
    `request suitable employment`
    `provide suitable employment`
    `conduct a work capacity assessment`
    `make the notification records available`

-- 1998 Act s 44(2), (4). Clock: hours, from the employer becoming aware of the workplace injury. "The employer of an
-- injured worker must notify the insurer or the Nominal Insurer within 48 hours after becoming aware that a worker has
-- received a workplace injury in the manner prescribed by the regulations" (Regulation cl 35(1): electronically, by the
-- approved form, or by telephone). Not "when the insurer is a self-insurer". Regulation cl 36: failing is an offence.
GIVEN `the employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 44(2) -- the employer must notify the insurer within 48 hours of becoming aware of the injury` IS
    IF `the employer is a self-insurer`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `notify the insurer of the workplace injury`
         WITHIN `the hours to notify the insurer (1998 Act s 44(2))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 44(2): the employer must notify the insurer within 48 hours after becoming aware of a workplace injury; Regulation cl 36 makes failing an offence (20 penalty units; penalty notice $550)"

-- 1998 Act s 44(1). Clock: hours, from the injury. "An injured worker must notify the employer that the worker has
-- received a workplace injury as soon as possible after the injury happens." No number of hours is set, so the duty never
-- falls due by time alone. When the worker notifies, the employer is aware, and its 48 hours run from then.
GIVEN `the employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 44 -- the worker must notify the employer as soon as possible, and the employer must then notify the insurer within 48 hours` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    MUST  `notify the employer of the workplace injury`
    HENCE `s 44(2) -- the employer must notify the insurer within 48 hours of becoming aware of the injury` `the employer is a self-insurer`

-- 1998 Act s 261. Clock: days, from the day time runs from (the injury, or under s 261(6), (7) the claimant's awareness).
-- Claiming is the claimant's choice (DO). Without a claim in 6 months compensation cannot be recovered unless an
-- exception applies: with reasonable cause, a claim within 3 years (s 261(4)(a)), or at any time for death or serious
-- and permanent disablement (s 261(4)(b)); otherwise only if the insurer determines to accept it (s 261(5)), which after
-- 3 years needs the Authority's approval. The seat works out the day counts.
GIVEN `the days in the 6 months` IS A NUMBER
      `the days in the 3 years` IS A NUMBER
      `the lateness is found to come from reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 261 -- a claim within 6 months, or only an exception lets compensation be recovered` IS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `make a claim for compensation`
    WITHIN `the days in the 6 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        IF `the lateness is found to come from reasonable cause` AND `the injury resulted in death or serious and permanent disablement`
        THEN PARTY `the worker`
             MAY   `make a claim for compensation`
        ELSE IF `the lateness is found to come from reasonable cause`
             THEN PARTY `the worker`
                  DO    `make a claim for compensation`
                  WITHIN (`the days in the 3 years` MINUS `the days in the 6 months`)
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST  BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 261(1), (4)(a): no claim within 3 years, and the injury did not result in death or serious and permanent disablement: compensation cannot be recovered unless the insurer, with the Authority's approval, determines to accept the claim (s 261(5))"
             ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
                  MAY   `determine to accept the late claim`

-- 1998 Act s 264(1), (4). Clock: days, from the employer receiving the claim or documentation. "An employer (not being a
-- self-insurer) who receives a claim or any other documentation in respect of a claim must, within 7 days after
-- receiving the claim or documentation, forward it to the employer's insurer. Maximum penalty -- 50 penalty units."
-- (4): no offence "if there was a reasonable excuse".
GIVEN `the employer is a self-insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 264(1) -- the employer must forward a claim to its insurer within 7 days` IS
    IF `the employer is a self-insurer`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `forward the claim to the insurer`
         WITHIN `the days to forward a claim (1998 Act s 264(1))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 264(1): the employer must forward a claim to its insurer within 7 days of receiving it; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100) unless there was a reasonable excuse (s 264(4))"

-- 1998 Act s 264(2). Clock: days, from the employer receiving the insurer's request. The employer "must, within 7 days
-- after receipt of the request, furnish the insurer with such of the specified information or documentation as is in the
-- employer's possession or reasonably obtainable by the employer. Maximum penalty -- 50 penalty units."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 264(2) -- the employer must give the insurer the information it requests within 7 days` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `give the insurer the information it requested`
    WITHIN `the days to give requested information (1998 Act s 264(2))`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 264(2): the employer must give the insurer the information or documents it requested within 7 days; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100) unless there was a reasonable excuse (s 264(4))"

-- 1998 Act ss 267-269. Clock: days, from the initial notification of the injury to the insurer (s 266). s 267(1):
-- "Provisional weekly payments of compensation by an insurer are to commence within 7 days after initial notification
-- ..., unless the insurer has a reasonable excuse"; (2): only an excuse "that the Workers Compensation Guidelines provide
-- is a reasonable excuse" (the Guidelines are not deposited: a FACT); (5): failing is an offence (50 penalty units).
-- s 268: with a reasonable excuse, the insurer "must within 7 days after receiving the initial notification of injury give
-- the worker notice in writing" with the excuse, a statement that the worker may claim and the claim "will be determined
-- within 21 days", and how to claim (50 penalty units). s 269: "As soon as practicable after" commencing, the insurer
-- "must give the worker a notice in writing" -- no number of days, so never due by time alone.
GIVEN `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `ss 267-269 -- the insurer must start provisional weekly payments within 7 days, or give notice of its reasonable excuse` IS
    IF `the insurer has a reasonable excuse under the Guidelines`
    THEN PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `give the worker written notice of the reasonable excuse`
         WITHIN `the days to give notice of a reasonable excuse (1998 Act s 268)`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 268: an insurer with a reasonable excuse for not starting provisional weekly payments must give the worker written notice of it within 7 days of the initial notification; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100)"
    ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `commence provisional weekly payments`
         WITHIN `the days to start provisional weekly payments (1998 Act s 267(1))`
         HENCE (PARTY `the insurer` MUST `give the worker notice of the s 269 matters`)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 267(1), (5): without a reasonable excuse the insurer must start provisional weekly payments within 7 days of the initial notification of the injury; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100)"

-- 1998 Act s 274. Clock: days, from the claim for weekly payments being made. The insurer must determine the claim within
-- 21 days by accepting liability and commencing weekly payments, or disputing liability (s 274(1)); or it may accept
-- liability provisionally for up to 12 weeks (s 274(2)), which extends the time to the end of that period (s 274(3)), and
-- the claim must then be finally determined (READING: within the weeks accepted, counted from the provisional
-- acceptance). s 274(4): no provisional acceptance under s 274 if provisional payments under Division 1 are already being
-- made; s 276(1) then extends the time to the end of that provisional period (the days left are a parameter: 0 if none).
-- s 283(1): failing to determine a claim "as and when required" is an offence (50 penalty units) unless the insurer has a
-- reasonable excuse the Guidelines recognise.
GIVEN `the determination` IS A `Claim determination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an allowed s 274(2) determination` `the determination` IS
    CONSIDER `the determination`
    WHEN `accepting liability provisionally for` `weeks` THEN `weeks` GREATER THAN 0 AND `weeks` AT MOST `the most weeks of provisional acceptance (1998 Act ss 267(3), 274(2))`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the determination` IS A `Claim determination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a final determination` `the determination` IS
    CONSIDER `the determination`
    WHEN `accepting liability provisionally for` `weeks` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `days left of provisional payments already being made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 274 -- the insurer must determine a claim for weekly payments within 21 days, or by the end of a provisional acceptance` IS
    IF `days left of provisional payments already being made` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `determine the claim for weekly payments` `final` PROVIDED `is a final determination` `final`
         WITHIN (max `the days to determine a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274(1))` `days left of provisional payments already being made`)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act ss 274(1), 276(1), 283(1): the insurer must determine the claim by accepting liability or disputing it within 21 days, or by the end of the provisional payments already being made if later; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100) without a reasonable excuse"
    ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `determine the claim for weekly payments` `how` PROVIDED `is an allowed s 274(2) determination` `how`
         WITHIN `the days to determine a claim for weekly payments (1998 Act s 274(1))`
         HENCE
             CONSIDER `how`
             WHEN `accepting liability provisionally for` `weeks` THEN
                 PARTY `the insurer`
                 MUST  `determine the claim for weekly payments` `final` PROVIDED `is a final determination` `final`
                 WITHIN (7 TIMES `weeks`)
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 274(3), 283(1): after a provisional acceptance the insurer must determine the claim by the end of the provisional period; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100) without a reasonable excuse"
             OTHERWISE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 274(1), 283(1): the insurer must determine a claim for weekly payments within 21 days, by accepting liability and commencing payments, disputing liability, or accepting provisionally for up to 12 weeks; an offence (50 penalty units; penalty notice $1,100) without a reasonable excuse"

-- 1998 Act ss 48, 48A. Clock: days, from the insurer giving the s 48A(2) notice. s 48(1): a worker with current work
-- capacity "must, in co-operation with the employer or insurer, make reasonable efforts to return to work"; the notice
-- names the obligation and a date 14 to 60 days ahead (s 48A(2)(b); the days are a parameter). A notice outside that range
-- (or without the reason and consequences) allows no suspension: the insurer must not suspend on it. Complying is the
-- worker's choice (DO). If the worker does not comply by the date, the insurer may suspend for 28 days (s 48A(3)); if the
-- worker complies within them, the insurer must resume from that day (s 48A(4), no number of days); if not, the insurer
-- may terminate weekly payments (s 48A(6)), or cease and determine the entitlement where s 48A(7)(b) is met.
GIVEN `the days from the notice to the date it specifies` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `ss 48, 48A -- a worker given a return to work notice complies by the date, or weekly payments may be suspended and then ended` IS
    IF NOT (    `the notice states the reason, the obligation and the consequences`
            AND `the days from the notice to the date it specifies` AT LEAST `the fewest days to the date in a s 48A notice`
            AND `the days from the notice to the date it specifies` AT MOST `the most days to the date in a s 48A notice`)
    THEN PARTY `the insurer`
         SHANT `suspend weekly payments`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 48A(1)-(2): the insurer may suspend only in accordance with s 48A, after a written notice stating the reason, the obligation, the consequences and a date at least 14 and no more than 60 days after the notice"
    ELSE PARTY `the worker`
         DO    `comply with the s 48 obligation in the notice`
         WITHIN `the days from the notice to the date it specifies`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST
             PARTY `the worker`
             DO    `comply with the s 48 obligation in the notice`
             WITHIN `the days of a s 48A suspension`
             HENCE (PARTY `the insurer` MUST `resume weekly payments from the day the worker complied`)
             LEST
                 IF `in the 12 months before the notice: 2 notices without a suspension, or 1 suspension`
                 THEN PARTY `the insurer`
                      MAY   `cease and determine the entitlement to weekly payments by written notice`
                 ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
                      MAY   `terminate weekly payments by written notice`

-- 1998 Act s 49. Clock: days, from the worker being able to return to work. Asking is the worker's choice (DO); once
-- asked, the employer must provide suitable employment (s 49(1), 50 penalty units). The Act sets no number of days, so
-- the duty never falls due by time alone. No duty where s 49(3) applies.
GIVEN `an exception in s 49(3) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 49 -- at the worker's request, the employer must provide suitable employment` IS
    IF `an exception in s 49(3) applies`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the worker`
         DO    `request suitable employment`
         HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
                MUST  `provide suitable employment`
                LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "1998 Act s 49(1): at the request of a worker able to return to work, the employer liable to pay compensation must provide suitable employment; an offence (50 penalty units)")
         LEST  FULFILLED

-- 1987 Act s 38(4)-(5). Clock: days, from the start of the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period. The insurer must
-- ensure an assessment "during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period, and ... thereafter at least once every
-- 2 years" (the recursion); not for a worker with highest needs unless the insurer thinks it appropriate and the worker
-- asks (s 38(5)). The 2-year clock is 730 days (READING).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 38(4)(b) -- the insurer must ensure a work capacity assessment at least once every 2 years` IS
    PARTY `the insurer`
    MUST  `conduct a work capacity assessment`
    WITHIN `the days in 2 years for s 38(4)(b)`
    HENCE (`s 38(4)(b) -- the insurer must ensure a work capacity assessment at least once every 2 years`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1987 Act s 38(4)(b): after the second entitlement period the insurer must ensure a work capacity assessment at least once every 2 years"

GIVEN `a worker with highest needs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker asked for an assessment and the insurer thinks it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `s 38(4), (5) -- the insurer must ensure work capacity assessments, except for a worker with highest needs` IS
    IF `a worker with highest needs`
    THEN IF `the worker asked for an assessment and the insurer thinks it appropriate`
         THEN PARTY `the insurer`
              MAY   `conduct a work capacity assessment`
         ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
              SHANT `conduct a work capacity assessment`
              LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1987 Act s 38(5): an insurer is not to conduct a work capacity assessment of a worker with highest needs unless it thinks it appropriate and the worker requests it"
    ELSE PARTY `the insurer`
         MUST  `conduct a work capacity assessment`
         WITHIN `the last day of the last 52 weeks, counted from their first day`
         HENCE (`s 38(4)(b) -- the insurer must ensure a work capacity assessment at least once every 2 years`)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the insurer` BECAUSE "1987 Act s 38(4)(a): the insurer must ensure a work capacity assessment during the last 52 weeks of the second entitlement period"

-- Regulation cl 35(3). Clock: days, from the request by an inspector (s 238 of the 1998 Act) or an authorised employee
-- representative. The employer "must make the records kept under subclause (2) available for inspection ... no later than
-- 7 days after the date of" the request. Maximum penalty -- 20 penalty units.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WC party` `WC act`
DECIDE `Regulation cl 35(3) -- the employer must make its notification records available within 7 days of a request` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `make the notification records available`
    WITHIN `the days to make the notification records available (Regulation cl 35(3))`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "Regulation cl 35(3): the employer must make its records of the injury notification available no later than 7 days after a request by an inspector or an authorised employee representative; an offence (20 penalty units)"
